export abstract anchor FactoryQuestions:
    questions:
        Questions are open, answered, withdrawn, or closed. Answers are
        current, superseded, or rejected. A question records its order, asker,
        decision key, generation, and blocking scope. The scope is a set of seed
        steps plus all transitive dependents, recomputed whenever the plan
        changes. Questions are same-order only; cross-order effects use a
        successor order.
        An answer presents the expected generation. A mismatch returns a
        conflict and applies nothing. An identical answer is a no-op. Different
        answers for one generation are rejected as a conflict and the engineer
        confirms. A new answer to an answered question creates a new generation,
        supersedes the old answer, and triggers revalidation. Rejected answers
        remain in the audit.
        Withdrawal requires the engineer or an explicit delegate, except a
        verified moot question whose scoped steps are all terminal. A withdrawn
        question reopens only as a new generation. Only the engineer or an
        explicit delegate answers. Agent help requests are a separate operation.
        Before completion every open question is answered, withdrawn, or carried
        into a named successor. After completion new questions require a
        successor order. Duplicate questions share a decision key; the newest
        open question is active and the rest are linked.
    changedAnswers:
        Briefs and results record the question generations and assumption
        records they rely on. An assumption records its statement, provenance,
        scope, owner, and state.
        A changed answer traces the recorded assumptions and dependency edges
        that consumed an earlier generation, including transitive dependents,
        and records examined but unaffected results as negative evidence. A
        revalidation is bound to the answer generation and states the result
        revision it examined. It presents the order aggregate version and is
        checked against the latest generation before commit; an older-generation
        decision is superseded. Revalidations are idempotent by request
        identifier.
        Results that still satisfy the answer are kept with an explicit record.
        The rest are superseded, outputs preserved, and replacements planned by
        an authorized agent. Running work under the old generation is paused or
        superseded and its outputs preserved. An active order is corrected in
        place; a completed order gets a successor order carrying the evidence.
        An answer that changes intent is confirmed by the engineer or an
        explicitly delegated order owner. Criteria are re-frozen before
        replacement work, and a fresh independent assessor applies them.
